[ORDINAL] of all, even though [ORGANIZATION] Manager is easier to learn, [Mod Organizer](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[PERSON]?) is a better alternative. It installs mods in a separated folder from game files, so you will have less issues if your mod setup doesn't work. That said, you can start modding with [ORGANIZATION] if you want at [ORDINAL], just think about switching over to [LOCATION] if you start installing lots of stuff.

Something really important: use [LOOT](https://loot.github.io/) to sort your mod load order after having installed a few of them.

To start, install [SKSE](http://skse.silverlock.org/), it's required for most mods now. Then, [SkyUI](http://www.nexusmods.com/[PRODUCT]mods/3863/?) should be your [ORDINAL] mod, it's a requirement for [QUANTITY] of other mods and has a better mouse/keyboard [ORGANIZATION]. If you want to keep the classic menus (to play with a controller for instance), install [SkyUI Away](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[LOCATION]?).

Now, if you've got the dlcs, install [Unofficial Skyrim Legendary patch](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/71214/?). It's a mod that has a lot of fixes to glitches and problems that were not fixed by [LOCATION]. If you only have the vanilla game, or not all the dlcs, install the other versions ([vanilla](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[PRODUCT]?), [Dragonborn](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[LOCATION]?), [Dawnguard](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/23491/?), [Heartfire](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/25127/?)).

If you're playing with mouse and keyboard, install [Better Dialogue Controls](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/27371/?) and [Better MessageBox Controls](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[ORGANIZATION]?) to make your life easier navigating the menus and selecting options.


Now, some mods to improve the game overall: 

- [Immersive HUD - iHUD](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/3222/?) allows to show or hide and customize the [ORGANIZATION];

- [Enhanced Camera](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/57859/?): see your character's body in [ORDINAL] person;

- [VioLens - A Killmove Mod](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/56980/?): customize your killmoves;

- [Customizable Camera](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[LOCATION]?): customize your camera options;

- [[WORK_OF_ART]/skyrim/mods/17214/?): removes the stupid little dance npcs make when dying;

- [Main Menu](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/64948/?): see more info about the save you're loading;

- [[PERSON]?): there are other follower mods but this one is great, allows you to have  ahuge range of options for them;

- [[PERSON]/skyrim/mods/69541/?): adds a lot more dialogue to followers;

- [Timing is Everything](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/38151/?): gives you control over a lot of quests so that you can delay them or start them earlier;

- [Run For Your Lives](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/23906/?): non-fighters npcs will stop playing heroes when attacked by dragons and flee instead, [When Vampires Attack](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/28235/?) does the same thing for vampire attacks.


Some other mods I like: 

- [Simply Knock](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/73236/?): you can knock on npcs' doors and they can let you in (if they want to), which is super useful sometimes;

- [Quick Loot](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[PERSON]?): allows you to loot stuff from containers/corpses or whatever without opening the menu, has a reskin with better [ORGANIZATION] as well;

- [Combat Evolved](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/56147/?): a great mod to enhance enemy AI that works both with vanilla and combat mods, [CARDINAL] of my favorites;

- [All Geared Up](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/[NORP]?): you can see all the weapons you have equipped on your character;

- [[PRODUCT] Unbound](http://www.nexusmods.com/skyrim/mods/71465/?): an alternate start mod that lets you configure tons of options (like being dragonborn or not) and your starting location, or even make everything random.

Anyway, these are some great mods, not all essentials, but they should improve on the vanilla game.

